      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A lot of this is already available using animator state machines. The developers are working on a visual scripting system that will replace the current trigger system called udon. So what you are asking for is coming.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-16T14:42:56.170Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Additional to VRC_Trigger, add some simple \"condition\" feature to run that trigger!\nlike, if variable A is greater than ~, equal to ~, and so on!\nthis can be used for lots of 'game' type worlds.\n\n\nEdit: more specifically,\nthis 'condition' system will need additionally 'variable' function and some trigger that can change the variable (Set/Add/Sub/Del Variable Action or by UI like a slider)\n[1] Num type condition\nbasic and can be used broadly. (less than ~, greater than ~) can be mixed, equal to ~.\n[2] String type condition\nactually not necessary, but if you have a mind to add this it'll only need equal to condition and trigger that can add string messages.\n[3] Interactive type condition\nthis is more complexed than others, usually use with collider so it checks if the player's in a specific area, or holding some pickable object, and so on.\n[4] Time type condition\ntimer, like 10 minutes after the game ends.",
